#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175625 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b934301a-aa9f-5ed6-9a31-e05391d1913c" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11010" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cot x$?\n\n1. The function has zeros at $x = \\pi n$, where $n$ is an integer.\n2. The function has asymptotes at $x = \\pm\\dfrac \\pi 2, \\pm \\dfrac {3 \\pi} 2,\\dots$\n3. The range of $y = \\cot x$ is $[MATH: (-\\infty,-1] \\cup [1,\\infty).]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cot x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3566/Source/Images/6f4d4cece7d2e9fef3be78e1564aaa4e.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros of the function occur at the values $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$.\n- Statement II is false. The vertical asymptotes of the function are at integer multiples of $\\pi$, i.e., $x=n\\pi$.\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=\\cot x$ is $(-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175626 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d4ebf4f8-d45a-5657-9331-1a6867110288" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11011" :question/problem "If $\\cot x = 1$ for some $x$, then find the value of $\\cot(x+5\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "The period of $y = \\cot x$ is $\\pi$. Therefore, for any integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n\\cot{x} = \\cot{(x+n\\pi)}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cot x &= \\cot (x + 5 \\cdot π) \\\\\n&= \\cot (x + 5π)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if\n\n$$\n\\cot{x} = 1\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\cot{(x+5\\pi)} = 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175631 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "2c8233f9-6749-5244-a209-6bf41b64388f" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11016" :question/problem "If $\\cot x = 2$, then what is the value of $\\cot (-x+7\\pi)$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\cot{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3566/Source/Images/bab1cfa649007237d6c54ebc22aa3e68.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\cot{x}$ is $\\pi$.\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\cot{x}$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n$\\cot(-x) = -\\cot{x}$.\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\cot{x}$, we have\n$\\cot (-x + 7π)|= \\cot (-x + π \\cdot 7); = \\cot (-x)$.\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\cot{x}$, we have\n$\\cot (-x)|=-\\cot x; =-2$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\cot (-x+7\\pi)=-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42852455-1abd-5fae-bf27-b7522a46d316" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247301} {:answer/id #uuid "99668bc9-84f4-519d-a307-6e4280b55e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247302} {:answer/id #uuid "4f43a53f-0d0c-5877-88b2-ebe4caee3b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247303} {:answer/id #uuid "10486fac-99c3-56f9-964d-483dbf01b69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247304} {:answer/id #uuid "955525c5-0064-5e8b-ada0-7a14cab9da6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f43a53f-0d0c-5877-88b2-ebe4caee3b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247303} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dbd4702-9535-5dbf-a2d8-d24331024d34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247300}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3bd598c-63a0-5a17-b0d7-635b8c58e036" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103836" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cot⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$\n- The domain of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n- The period of the function is $\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/7785ad73f6e5212772c3053780ffd055f37cfb39927b6ddc3e40cd3a55b8ba4e.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The vertical asymptotes of the function are integer multiples of $\\pi $, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The domain of the function is all real numbers except the values where the asymptotes occur, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59fb46b0-1b36-5f68-8844-d17e65035d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247308} {:answer/id #uuid "35ea3826-7d82-54f8-bda5-d89049cc066b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247309} {:answer/id #uuid "afcbf2f0-9da4-5cb3-b04a-55a2daf28deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247310} {:answer/id #uuid "2e25e5e8-6ea9-5ef7-a723-df6aff48c3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247311} {:answer/id #uuid "ac34bc36-731a-512b-8623-09a169356be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac34bc36-731a-512b-8623-09a169356be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247312} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ad3f871-fbd3-5873-89e4-85da89ec0bd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247307}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3621c087-2f4f-5afd-9fb1-a602cf08aa35" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103838" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=-4$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $3cot⁡(x+17\\pi )+6.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=17$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x & =cot⁡(x+17\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cot⁡(x+17\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=-4,$ then $cot⁡(x+17\\pi )=-4.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3cot⁡(x+7\\pi )+6 & =3(-4)+6 \\\\  & =-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edbebaf8-ee68-573f-9f56-efaadee04c00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247315} {:answer/id #uuid "5e97bfef-6bd5-5095-9063-7aeb18e6d44b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247316} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6ed830-864a-5ce7-bfd6-40421cddf26f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247317} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1e0cc8-3b2e-57c9-93e5-a470cdc964a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247318} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6af019-5fc5-5049-a27a-32b4ca3787d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edbebaf8-ee68-573f-9f56-efaadee04c00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247315} :answer-field/id #uuid "c88a0459-bc86-5cf5-9a1d-f69d4ca08bee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247314}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f045e7f-116d-56a9-8dbb-f27a1858db53" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103839" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{5}$ for some $x$, then find the value of $2\\sqrt{5}cot⁡(x-3\\pi )-8.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-3$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x=cot⁡(x+(-3)\\cdot \\pi )=cot⁡(x-3\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{5},$ then $cot⁡(x-3\\pi )=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5}cot⁡(x-3\\pi )-8 & =2\\sqrt{5}(\\sqrt{5})-8 \\\\  & =2{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}-8 \\\\  & =10-8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca13301-f322-5966-8c1b-376a73243ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247322} {:answer/id #uuid "cb154967-200b-5d5b-ba5e-fb9baf60dd57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247323} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1efcc5-b35d-570f-8b89-5ff3d3695003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247324} {:answer/id #uuid "075b92fc-62d2-5972-8698-021a9deab6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247325} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd8210e-432f-5628-84f3-b75eecf78ce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ca13301-f322-5966-8c1b-376a73243ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247322} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f5f1f24-472b-58a2-9257-623454bbfa2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247321}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb31ed8f-b730-5095-8215-7e8243b3e537" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103840" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{2}$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $cot⁡(x-9\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x & =cot⁡(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cot⁡(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ then $cot⁡(x-9\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efa56ad-5cac-581d-87f5-daf6e5b8e8c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247329} {:answer/id #uuid "232b36d0-235e-581c-ad5f-a1ce7c1001f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247330} {:answer/id #uuid "43754cfc-c3dd-515d-ba83-cd68897b2d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247331} {:answer/id #uuid "cd74a48e-9f91-55d3-88f9-ddf0f38ff5b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247332} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5bbc22-46ca-5577-b870-6c69749bd7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd74a48e-9f91-55d3-88f9-ddf0f38ff5b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247332} :answer-field/id #uuid "db81b4bc-5a86-5f30-8343-97b7fbfaf2e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247328}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "39378440-a829-50ce-ab74-9b393b345cdc" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-136559" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\frac{1}{4},$ then $4cot⁡(-x+4\\pi )+1=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x+4\\pi ) & =cot⁡(-x+\\pi \\cdot 4) \\\\  & =cot⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x) & =-cot⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4cot⁡(-x+4\\pi )+1 & =4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})+1 \\\\  & =-1+1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19106f83-a765-54a1-bcd4-44e38c4af8c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247336} {:answer/id #uuid "846bd378-a8ad-50b9-8ae3-37cb5f8cdb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247337} {:answer/id #uuid "17bddba3-e3c9-5cf2-86d9-d985f07f0455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247338} {:answer/id #uuid "cb371677-6735-5966-815b-8a1e780f0ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247339} {:answer/id #uuid "febef15b-2577-5766-982d-569e653649c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "846bd378-a8ad-50b9-8ae3-37cb5f8cdb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247337} :answer-field/id #uuid "44c42671-cdeb-5615-aa9a-087af04a7e1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247335}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e58dfc80-f6ad-5a11-abf6-6aa35aa5a15b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-136588" :question/problem "If $cot⁡a=-9,$ then $cot⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-a) & =-cot⁡a \\\\  & =-(-9) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b27ea71-5ce6-53ed-91b6-4f1be8956513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247343} {:answer/id #uuid "f529e2d4-ffe5-53f5-bcd9-6fea86ccbd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247344} {:answer/id #uuid "fafad114-c4f2-579f-989b-84fdffc9def9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247345} {:answer/id #uuid "2284a17f-ff98-552a-9f2d-64a4ffe2d3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247346} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0e1fba-8ed5-51f6-b296-8727a2b28c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f529e2d4-ffe5-53f5-bcd9-6fea86ccbd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247344} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc21ffd8-dc80-5967-870f-d35d16117a7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247342}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5e3292b-1bdc-5b00-9b1b-faad502214e0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158055" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\frac{5}{2},$ then $cot⁡(-x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x) & =-cot⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "492b497a-66c3-5ff5-a2b4-36e04d3a10ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247350} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cc35cf-8575-56a8-9e81-952bf35f531e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7+5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247351} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa752de-7887-5e91-ada4-ede9bfbda66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247352} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad87590-d7b6-5330-b313-6018715d09ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247353} {:answer/id #uuid "220ee753-4257-5253-8b24-283f054d1852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fa752de-7887-5e91-ada4-ede9bfbda66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247352} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ad0e85-c363-5a3f-8ae2-9a9004fa5fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247349}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eaefe6c3-4e7d-5448-aa59-5c5d0ac1b47f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158058" :question/problem "If $cot⁡a=-7,$ then $cot⁡(-a+5\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-a+5\\pi ) & =cot⁡(-a+\\pi \\cdot 5) \\\\  & =cot⁡(-a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-a) & =-cot⁡a \\\\  & =-(-7) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $cot⁡(-a+5\\pi )=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0251566-4dfc-5786-b00a-ce609e5b2698" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e68efc37-76bd-5bf6-b743-dfd9175fb662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247357} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd474d-8edf-5a20-bd41-3b9bb8bf6c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247358} {:answer/id #uuid "44319073-b4a4-5787-974d-f4464f0b9c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247359} {:answer/id #uuid "272313f8-15d3-51d4-8778-da840725cc5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247360} {:answer/id #uuid "4655306f-1cfe-5f48-8eb3-32a1507f30d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd474d-8edf-5a20-bd41-3b9bb8bf6c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247358} :answer-field/id #uuid "45381627-3350-56fc-b734-814db14cb640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247356}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a2d1494-b0ea-5ce1-b4dc-41e0b949e25d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158064" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=-6,$ then $\\frac{1}{2}cot⁡(-x+15\\pi )+7=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/6eb672fe024f024f20c7c3c80947d1b47bade8f998e705d6f411ae3f298ecde2.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $cot⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡(-x)=-cot⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x+15\\pi ) & =cot⁡(-x+\\pi \\cdot 15) \\\\  & =cot⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $cot⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡(-x) & =-cot⁡x \\\\  & =-(-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}cot⁡(-x+15\\pi )+7 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6+7 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2}+7 \\\\  & =3+7 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "674e8da5-fde8-5019-b9cf-83facc4c70c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the value $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247364} {:answer/id #uuid "fdae6056-f0da-5d4f-8313-f58ac0b8a423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the values $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247365} {:answer/id #uuid "9dca25cb-99c1-5e6f-a6d7-434ee96044b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the values $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247366} {:answer/id #uuid "5678fbd7-7c49-540f-bc64-4bf8cf9fe517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the values $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247367} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4d140c-c318-56f2-8fff-f710524e03ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the values $x=2n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdae6056-f0da-5d4f-8313-f58ac0b8a423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers except the values $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247365} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d030757-557b-51e3-a658-09cb25d5e7a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247363}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "220292be-47cd-50fc-8fcf-9424f1806fe8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-27910" :question/problem "What is the domain of $y=cot⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/22674bef9e806fca07026b8d441877c251761de4c64cc005eed912e62a34ce67.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function $y=cot⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the values $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1faa8ba2-aebc-5691-972f-69b40138a5c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247371} {:answer/id #uuid "67fbfe1a-c28f-5286-bce4-fe71538f6901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247372} {:answer/id #uuid "1d18e03d-2ce5-5c91-b812-a8e304d25707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247373} {:answer/id #uuid "84110eb1-8a22-5318-8c94-0473ce116fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247374} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f8c56a-0269-5357-91b3-633423027ee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1faa8ba2-aebc-5691-972f-69b40138a5c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247371} :answer-field/id #uuid "77eabd8c-9b81-5e2f-a754-e1a7ecc52056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d388aac2-9989-51c3-b23b-5c3e41da021d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-27946" :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the asymptotes of $y=cot⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/22674bef9e806fca07026b8d441877c251761de4c64cc005eed912e62a34ce67.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the graph occur at integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of $y=cot⁡x$ occur at $x=n\\pi $ for integer $n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a6a285-8d9f-5a7b-8e1a-7135661fdbc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247378} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc5cd1f-23a8-5186-a1ad-2f72f56dc41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247379} {:answer/id #uuid "0f531995-1bc4-5b32-a6e6-e9a6b016b95e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247380} {:answer/id #uuid "7693f898-6124-5580-a695-c75ffc1d8751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247381} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca24f42-91ed-5dc9-bea1-8bddae3e3671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6a6a285-8d9f-5a7b-8e1a-7135661fdbc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247378} :answer-field/id #uuid "6affbe6b-8ee4-5b11-afb9-c2624131016d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247377}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "443dc7a5-6d47-5569-a781-301d4f9b84b7" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-42933" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cot⁡x?$\n\n- The period is $\\pi .$ $$\n- It is increasing over $(0,\\pi ).$\n- $x=\\pi $ is a zero." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/22674bef9e806fca07026b8d441877c251761de4c64cc005eed912e62a34ce67.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is decreasing over $(0,\\pi ).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not defined at $x=\\pi .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5c18004-772b-59d0-aa2b-8e0bd93c4f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247385} {:answer/id #uuid "55c17395-5e86-56c5-865f-e429419f1770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247386} {:answer/id #uuid "012e802c-a345-53df-8df8-f3db7d16b580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247387} {:answer/id #uuid "10120ab3-d383-593a-9b86-7648ffd0640e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247388} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ecd11-9fdc-554b-bf77-33c91c7301a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10120ab3-d383-593a-9b86-7648ffd0640e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247388} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0a2ea5-c635-5fb8-970c-d61ad82bd53d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247384}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4e0627c-7ad9-5c01-b554-599190d7bd8d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-66675" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{3}$ for some $x$, then find the value of $\\sqrt{3}cot⁡(x-\\pi )-4.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-1$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x=cot⁡(x+(-1)\\cdot \\pi )=cot⁡(x-\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=\\sqrt{3},$ then $cot⁡(x-\\pi )=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}cot⁡(x-\\pi )-4 & =\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3})-4 \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =3-4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f4e32f-b5ff-5bda-a78d-e17346853b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247392} {:answer/id #uuid "34e43c7e-8758-577d-9140-107f40124a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247393} {:answer/id #uuid "6cbb2e28-8edf-5a07-bf8a-8dc623c6395c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247394} {:answer/id #uuid "052bdebf-1892-58f2-89c5-8da067810680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247395} {:answer/id #uuid "b85c647f-82cb-534e-b8e1-a32f0af5a54f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e43c7e-8758-577d-9140-107f40124a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247393} :answer-field/id #uuid "f64ffa6c-1d9e-5cd4-93bb-384309b9a9aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247391}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afeaf4fc-dbfe-5597-a62c-d8cecbf34d0e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70669" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cot⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has no minimum value. $$\n- $x=-4\\pi $ is in the domain of the function. $$\n- $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/8bc549c68a3bc5b7989ac1835e4bb58183066c7797264b8cccd4f3fd2c895056.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has no minimum or maximum value. $$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $n\\pi $ for any integer $n$, thus it is not defined for $x=-4\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The zeros of $y=cot⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n.$ Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d02418c3-4c04-57b8-8f10-18858b1759ab" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dad4a2ba-551d-5a73-9933-bd2907a89835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247399} {:answer/id #uuid "36e74d09-989f-5b5c-8071-e24954ac7168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247400} {:answer/id #uuid "273b3f39-bed2-5d0b-9d63-86730ed6225d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247401} {:answer/id #uuid "0d682641-e746-5034-9194-86287d33704f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247402} {:answer/id #uuid "fd93ede5-3ec6-53b5-af34-27f5d1d466d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36e74d09-989f-5b5c-8071-e24954ac7168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247400} :answer-field/id #uuid "659bdd5b-e748-566d-94ba-ccedf1752fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247398}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7c77765-9446-57cc-b4ad-f8b00f72caf2" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70676" :question/problem "If $cot⁡x=1$ for some $x$, then find the value of $cot⁡(x+4\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncot⁡x=cot⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=4$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot⁡x=cot⁡(x+4\\cdot \\pi )=cot⁡(x+4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot⁡x=1,$ then $cot⁡(x+4\\pi )=1.$"}]}
